# Paper Reading Agent Workflow

All workflow instructions, generated notes, and tracker-related text must be in English.

## Reading mode
FAST is the default.

DEEP overrides FAST whenever the user explicitly requests deep reading, theorem-by-theorem analysis, proof reconstruction, exhaustive analysis, reproducibility analysis, appendix inspection, or a full critical review.

If FAST and DEEP are both mentioned, use DEEP.

Use:
- `skills/paper-deep-reading/SKILL.md`
- `skills/paper-tracker/SKILL.md`

## Tracker statuses
Use exactly:
- 🔴 To read
- 🟡 Review ready
- 🟢 Done

## Reading workflow
When asked to read a paper in `reading_queue.md`:
1. Identify the exact paper and registry record.
2. Determine FAST or DEEP.
3. Use `paper-deep-reading`.
4. Save the note under the appropriate `notes/<project>/` folder.
5. After the note exists:
   - update `reading_queue.md`
   - update `data/paper_registry.json`
   - set status to `🟡 Review ready`
   - add the note link
6. Commit only files touched by this task.
7. Do not push automatically unless the user explicitly authorizes pushing in the current session.
8. If committed locally, tell the user to run `git push`.

## Marking Done
Only when the user explicitly confirms they reviewed/finished/approved the paper:
- change status to `🟢 Done` in both queue and registry
- preserve the note link
- commit only relevant files
- do not push automatically unless explicitly authorized

## Discovery
Weekly discovery must:
- never duplicate registered papers
- preserve status and notes
- add only genuinely unseen papers as `🔴 To read`
- refresh metadata without resetting state

